5. API reproducibility and provenance audit (G1.4, corrected)

5.1 Provenance operationalization

The v2.0.0 release notes confirm:

· AlphaGenome 2 model API (alphagenome.models.v2), supporting reference-condition and single-cell expression-conditioned predictions, variant and interval scoring, cell embeddings, and input gradients;
· Enhancer-to-gene scoring and calling utilities (alphagenome.interpretation.enhancer_scoring);
· filter_to_observed helper on TrackData and JunctionData.

There is no documented per-prediction is_imputed, provenance_source, or confidence_weight field in the release notes. The provenance audit therefore targets filter_to_observed, not hypothetical metadata fields.

5.2 Audit protocol

Phase 1 — filter_to_observed capability test. On a standardized suite of 500 loci across three representative conditions (K562, GM12878, primary CD4+ T cells):

1. Full-observation query → apply filter_to_observed → record surviving track set.
2. Partial-observation query (e.g., chromatin accessibility only) → re-apply filter_to_observed → record surviving track set.
3. The difference in surviving sets is the empirical imputed set.

Pass: stable, non-empty observed subset across loci and conditions. Fail: no filtering, empty return, or error → provenance unverified, H3 downgraded to observational.

Phase 2 — Controlled masking and validity gates C1/C2. For each modality m \in \{\text{RNA-seq, ATAC-seq, ChIP-seq}\}:

1. Compute S_{\text{obs}}(v,c,m) with all modalities provided.
2. Compute S_{\text{mask}}(v,c,m) with modality m withheld via the API's designated masking parameters.
3. C1: \mathrm{JSD}(P_{\text{obs}}\parallel P_{\text{mask}}) \le \tau_{\mathrm{JSD}} = 0.25; no NaN/infinite outputs; masked-output distribution not collapsed or outside observed-input distribution.
4. C2: zero variance in non-targeted metadata fields across paired calls; pinned client version ag2-client==2.0.0 logged in every request header.

