6. Evidence-score specification and leakage controls (G1.5, corrected)

6.1 Component definitions

Stability. Let \hat{y}_{v,c}^{(k)} denote the predicted effect across K=20 stochastic forward passes or perturbed input windows:

\mathrm{Stability}(v) = 1 - \frac{\sigma(\hat{y}_{v,c}^{(1)},\dots,\hat{y}_{v,c}^{(K)})}{|\mu(\hat{y}_{v,c})|+\epsilon},

with \epsilon = 10^{-4}, clipped to [0,1].

Concordance. Directional agreement across predicted modalities:

\mathrm{Concordance}(v) = \frac{1}{|M|-1}\sum_{m\in M}\mathbb{1}\left[\operatorname{sign}(\hat{y}_{v,c,m})=\operatorname{sign}(\hat{y}_{v,c,\text{primary}})\right].

Provenance. Ordinal weight from filter_to_observed status:

\mathrm{Provenance}(v)=
\begin{cases}
1.0 & \text{directly observed}\\
0.5 & \text{user-supplied / unverified}\\
0.0 & \text{model-imputed}
\end{cases}

Distance uncertainty.

\mathrm{DistanceUncertainty}(v) = \log\!\left(1+\frac{d_v}{d_0}\right),

with d_0=10 kb, min–max normalized on development data to [0,1].

6.2 Leakage controls — four freezing requirements

L1 — Stochastic pass parameters frozen. The RNG seed, number of passes K=20, and any input perturbation kernel are written to config/evidence_weights_v2.json. If the passes are generated with a seed chosen after seeing evaluation-set stability distributions, the Stability score is tuned to the evaluation set. Freeze before inspection.

L2 — Primary modality map frozen. "\hat{y}_{v,c,\text{primary}}" is undefined in v0.2. The frozen map is:

Estimand Primary modality
eQTL RNA-seq
caQTL ATAC/DNase
sQTL RNA-seq
enhancer perturbation RNA-seq

No per-variant selection of primary modality.

L3 — Development/evaluation k separation. Weight optimization uses k_{\text{dev}} \in \{50, 200\}; evaluation uses k_{\text{eval}} \in \{100, 500\}. No overlap. If weights are optimized at k=100 and evaluated at k=100, ER@k is partially in-sample.

L4 — Normalization constants frozen. Development-set means \mu_i^{\text{dev}} and standard deviations \sigma_i^{\text{dev}} for each component are written to the config file alongside the weights.

