7. Hypotheses and pre-specified decision rules

H1 — Distance-dependent magnitude miscalibration

Define e_{v,c}=y^{\text{exp}}_{v,c}-\hat{y}_{v,c}. The mixed model:

e_{v,c}=\alpha+\gamma_1\tilde{y}_{v,c}+\gamma_2\tilde{d}_v+\gamma_3\tilde{y}_{v,c}\tilde{d}_v+u_c+\epsilon_{v,c},

with standardized predictors \tilde{y} and \tilde{d}=\log(1+d_v); standardization constants published. \gamma_3 is the primary parameter: it tests whether magnitude error depends on distance.

AG1 vs AG2 comparison.

\Delta\gamma_3 = \gamma_3^{\mathrm{AG2}}-\gamma_3^{\mathrm{AG1}},

with a clustered bootstrap confidence interval. A difference in statistical significance between separate models is not evidence of a difference between models.

Decision structure.

Outcome Conditions
Support H1 (a) \gamma_3 significant at pre-specified \alpha; and (b) \(
Reject H1 (equivalence) Equivalence test rejects \gamma_3 \notin [-\delta^{\mathrm{eq}},+\delta^{\mathrm{eq}}] at \alpha (CI fully inside the equivalence interval), and \(
Inconclusive Neither of the above; reported as inconclusive, not forced into a binary

Small-cluster inference. Gene-clustered and locus-clustered standard errors are sensitivity analyses. If the number of independent clusters G<40, wild cluster bootstrap p-values replace asymptotic p-values as the primary test. Monte Carlo evidence shows the "rule of 42" is not reliable for unbalanced clusters, so the cluster-size distribution and minimum cluster size are reported explicitly, not just the count.

Distance definitions. TSS distance primary; enhancer-distance and gene-body-distance pre-specified sensitivity analyses. Definition-dependence is reported as a result, not resolved by choosing the favourable definition.

H2 — Cell-state conditioning

Matched cell-state conditioning improves predictive validity beyond bulk or biologically mismatched contexts. Primary metrics: DA, \rho_s, MAE, reported separately. Comparison against appropriate matched controls, not "no conditioning." Supported only if improvements exceed pre-specified MDEs from G1.3.

H3 — Modality provenance

Observed-versus-imputed provenance predicts differences in experimental reliability. Primary analysis observational (IRG) unless filter_to_observed is operational and C1/C2 pass, in which case CMAE provides a controlled model-input ablation. No causal biological interpretation is inferred from either result.

H4 — Evidence-based prioritization

Primary endpoint: diversity-constrained validation yield at pre-specified k. Secondary endpoint: biological utility. Decision structure now includes equivalence (correcting the v0.2 superiority-only test):

Outcome Condition
Support H4 \mathrm{ER}@k lower CI bound >1.18
Reject H4 (equivalence) \mathrm{ER}@k CI fully inside [0.90, 1.10]
Inconclusive CI excludes 1.0 but includes the MDE region, or crosses the equivalence boundary

Without this, a non-significant H4 result would be reported as "falsified" when it may simply be underpowered — the failure mode the falsification-first commitment was designed to prevent.

Component ablation — frozen.

Model Tests
Raw AG2 Baseline
Raw AG2 + stability Marginal value of stability
Raw AG2 + concordance Marginal value of concordance
Raw AG2 + provenance Marginal value of provenance
Raw AG2 + distance uncertainty Marginal value of distance
Full E(v) Combined
Full E(v) without provenance Incremental value of provenance given the rest
Full E(v) without stability Incremental value of stability given the rest
Full E(v) without concordance Incremental value of concordance given the rest
Full E(v) without distance Incremental value of distance given the rest

Decision rule. If removing provenance leaves ER@k (or \Delta@k) statistically and scientifically unchanged, provenance is not claimed as a demonstrated source of utility, even if the full score beats baseline. Interactions are explicitly permitted.

