8. Statistical analysis plan (G1.3, frozen)

MDEs at \alpha=0.05 two-tailed, power 1-\beta=0.80:

· H1: |\gamma_3^{\mathrm{MDE}}| \ge 0.12 standard deviations of error per log-distance unit.
· H2: \Delta\mathrm{DA} \ge 0.035; \Delta\mathrm{MAE} \ge 0.08\sigma_{y^{\text{exp}}}.
· H4: \mathrm{ER}@k \ge 1.18 under diversity constraints.

Equivalence margin (TOST) for H1: \delta^{\mathrm{eq}} = \pm 0.10, based on the biological noise floor of CRISPRi-FlowFISH and eQTL effect estimation. Equivalence declared iff the 90\% CI for \Delta\gamma_3 falls entirely within [-\delta^{\mathrm{eq}},+\delta^{\mathrm{eq}}].

Multiplicity. Primary hypotheses at \alpha=0.05; secondary subgroup analyses (distance quartiles, cell lineage, provenance status) via Benjamini–Hochberg at q\le 0.05.

Missing data. Complete-case logging; no imputation of experimental values.

Preregistration (G1.3b). OSF or equivalent, immutable timestamp, version bound to v0.3-frozen, submitted before evaluation-set inference.

